   world-war rows: the bigger side won 202 of 285 = 70.9%; the attacker was the bigger side in 87.0%; attackers won 67.0% (71.8% with more men, 35.1% with fewer); ranking by force ratio 0.67; if an attacker's chance owed nothing to numbers the bigger side would win 62.6%; agreement beyond that chance +0.22
